<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://lettyyang01.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://lettyyang01.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-13T00:16:24+00:00</updated><id>https://lettyyang01.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Letian Yang</title><subtitle>Exploring the world through data—I&apos;m Letian Yang, a PhD student in Statistics. This site is a collection of my academic journey, research insights and personal musings on all things statistical.</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Data Cleaning Checklist</title><link href="https://lettyyang01.github.io/blog/2026/data-cleaning/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Data Cleaning Checklist"/><published>2026-10-12T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-10-12T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://lettyyang01.github.io/blog/2026/data-cleaning</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://lettyyang01.github.io/blog/2026/data-cleaning/"><![CDATA[<p>Four phases: <strong>Inspect → Standardize → Repair → Verify</strong>. Three rules hold throughout:</p> <ul> <li>The raw file is never edited. Cleaning lives in code so it can be re-run.</li> <li>Profile before fixing. Every change should answer something you actually saw.</li> <li>Count what each step dropped or changed; that becomes the audit at the end.</li> </ul> <h2 id="1-inspect">1. Inspect</h2> <p>Look, don’t touch.</p> <h3 id="load-and-freeze">Load and freeze</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">raw</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">read_csv</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">data.csv</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>   <span class="c1"># or read_parquet / read_sql
</span><span class="n">df</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">raw</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">copy</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="n">n_raw</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nf">len</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">raw</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">raw</code> stays untouched as the baseline for every before/after comparison.</p> <h3 id="profile-the-table">Profile the table</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">shape</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">head</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">sample</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">5</span><span class="p">)</span>      <span class="c1"># head() hides problems further down
</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">info</span><span class="p">()</span>                     <span class="c1"># dtypes + non-null counts
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">describe</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">include</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">all</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>    <span class="c1"># numeric + categorical
</span>
<span class="c1"># missing rate per column
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">mean</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">sort_values</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">ascending</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">False</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">corr</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">numeric_only</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Look for numbers read as <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">object</code>, nearly empty columns, and ranges that make no sense.</p> <h3 id="profile-each-column">Profile each column</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="c1"># " NYC", "nyc" and "N/A" show up as separate values
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">city</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">value_counts</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dropna</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">False</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">city</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">nunique</span><span class="p">()</span>

<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">describe</span><span class="p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">value_counts(dropna=False)</code> on every categorical column is the fastest way to find formatting noise and disguised missing values.</p> <h2 id="2-standardize">2. Standardize</h2> <p>Make names, types and formats consistent so values become comparable.</p> <h3 id="column-names">Column names</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">columns</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">columns</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">strip</span><span class="p">()</span>
              <span class="p">.</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">lower</span><span class="p">()</span>
              <span class="p">.</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">replace</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">r</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">[^\w]+</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">_</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">regex</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="p">)</span>
<span class="n">df</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">rename</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">columns</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">{</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">cust_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">customer_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">})</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <h3 id="missing-placeholders">Missing placeholders</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">NA_TOKENS</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">""</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s"> </span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">NA</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">N/A</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">null</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">-</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">?</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">unknown</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span>
<span class="n">df</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">replace</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">NA_TOKENS</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">nan</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># numeric sentinels
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">age</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">age</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">replace</span><span class="p">({</span><span class="o">-</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">nan</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mi">999</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">nan</span><span class="p">})</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Do this before converting types. Otherwise <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">errors="coerce"</code> turns the placeholders into <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NaN</code> silently and you lose track of which ones were sentinels.</p> <h3 id="types-and-formats">Types and formats</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="c1"># text: whitespace and case
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">city</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">city</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">strip</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">title</span><span class="p">()</span>

<span class="c1"># numeric: strip symbols, then coerce
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nb">str</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">replace</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">r</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">[$,]</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">""</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">regex</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="bp">True</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">to_numeric</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">errors</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">coerce</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># dates
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">signup_date</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">pd</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">to_datetime</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">signup_date</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">errors</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">coerce</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># codes -&gt; labels
# unmapped values become NaN, so check value_counts first
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">gender</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">gender</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">map</span><span class="p">({</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">M</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">male</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">F</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">female</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">})</span>

<span class="c1"># how many values did coercion lose?
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">sum</span><span class="p">()</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="n">raw</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">sum</span><span class="p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Coercion never raises; it quietly produces <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">NaN</code>. Count the loss after each conversion.</p> <h3 id="duplicates">Duplicates</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">duplicated</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">sum</span><span class="p">()</span>                          <span class="c1"># exact copies
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">duplicated</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">subset</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">customer_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]).</span><span class="nf">sum</span><span class="p">()</span>    <span class="c1"># same key
</span>
<span class="c1"># keep the latest row per key
</span><span class="n">df</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span>
    <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">sort_values</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">updated_at</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
      <span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">drop_duplicates</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">subset</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">customer_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">keep</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">last</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>This comes after standardization: <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"NYC"</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">" nyc "</code> only become duplicates once formats agree. Decide explicitly which row survives, usually the latest.</p> <h2 id="3-repair">3. Repair</h2> <p>Decide what to do with the values that are absent or extreme.</p> <h3 id="missing-values">Missing values</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="c1"># is missingness random, or tied to another column?
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">mean</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">groupby</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">income</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">())[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">age</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">mean</span><span class="p">()</span>

<span class="c1"># drop a column that is mostly empty
</span><span class="n">df</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">drop</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">columns</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">fax</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">])</span>

<span class="c1"># drop rows missing a key field
</span><span class="n">df</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">dropna</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">subset</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">customer_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">signup_date</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">])</span>

<span class="c1"># keep a flag before filling: "was missing" is often informative
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">income_was_na</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">income</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">()</span>

<span class="c1"># median for skewed numeric, constant for categorical
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">income</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">income</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">fillna</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">income</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">median</span><span class="p">())</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">city</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">city</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">fillna</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">Unknown</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>For modeling, compute fill values on the training split only; otherwise the test set leaks into the imputer.</p> <h3 id="outliers">Outliers</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="c1"># IQR: robust to the outliers themselves
</span><span class="n">q1</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">q3</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">quantile</span><span class="p">([</span><span class="mf">0.25</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mf">0.75</span><span class="p">])</span>
<span class="n">iqr</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">q3</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="n">q1</span>
<span class="n">lo</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">hi</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">q1</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="mf">1.5</span> <span class="o">*</span> <span class="n">iqr</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">q3</span> <span class="o">+</span> <span class="mf">1.5</span> <span class="o">*</span> <span class="n">iqr</span>
<span class="n">is_out</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="o">~</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">between</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">lo</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">hi</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="c1"># z-score: assumes roughly normal data,
# and mean / std are themselves pulled by the outliers
</span><span class="n">z</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">mean</span><span class="p">())</span> <span class="o">/</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">std</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="n">is_out</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">z</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">abs</span><span class="p">()</span> <span class="o">&gt;</span> <span class="mi">3</span>

<span class="c1"># look before touching: entry error, unit mix-up, or real?
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="n">loc</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="n">is_out</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">customer_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]]</span>

<span class="c1"># then flag (safest), cap, or transform
</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price_outlier</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">is_out</span>

<span class="n">cap</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">quantile</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mf">0.99</span><span class="p">)</span>
<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">clip</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">upper</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="n">cap</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">log_price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">log1p</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">price</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">])</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Remove only confirmed errors. A real but extreme value is information, not noise.</p> <h2 id="4-verify">4. Verify</h2> <p>Prove the result is valid and that cleaning did not distort it.</p> <h3 id="validity-checks">Validity checks</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="k">assert</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">customer_id</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="n">is_unique</span>
<span class="k">assert</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">age</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">between</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="mi">120</span><span class="p">).</span><span class="nf">all</span><span class="p">()</span>
<span class="nf">assert </span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">end_date</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">&gt;=</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">start_date</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]).</span><span class="nf">all</span><span class="p">()</span>

<span class="n">total_ok</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">np</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">isclose</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">subtotal</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">]</span> <span class="o">+</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">tax</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">],</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">total</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">])</span>
<span class="k">assert</span> <span class="n">total_ok</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">all</span><span class="p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>Write the domain rules as <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">assert</code> so the pipeline fails loudly when new data breaks them.</p> <h3 id="audit-and-save">Audit and save</h3> <div class="language-python highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code><span class="n">dropped</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="mi">1</span> <span class="o">-</span> <span class="nf">len</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">)</span> <span class="o">/</span> <span class="n">n_raw</span>
<span class="nf">print</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sa">f</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">rows </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">n_raw</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> -&gt; </span><span class="si">{</span><span class="nf">len</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">df</span><span class="p">)</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> (</span><span class="si">{</span><span class="n">dropped</span><span class="si">:</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="o">%</span><span class="si">}</span><span class="s"> dropped)</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>

<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">isna</span><span class="p">().</span><span class="nf">mean</span><span class="p">()</span>      <span class="c1"># should be ~0 where you filled
</span>
<span class="n">pd</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nc">DataFrame</span><span class="p">({</span>
    <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">raw</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">raw</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">age</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">describe</span><span class="p">(),</span>
    <span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">clean</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">df</span><span class="p">[</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">age</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nf">describe</span><span class="p">(),</span>
<span class="p">})</span>

<span class="n">df</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nf">to_parquet</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="s">clean_2026-10-12.parquet</span><span class="sh">"</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div> <p>A large shift in mean or variance between <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">raw</code> and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">clean</code> means a step was too aggressive. Finally, wrap phases 2 to 4 in one <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">clean(raw)</code> function so the same cleaning runs on the next batch.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="notes"/><category term="pandas"/><category term="data-cleaning"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[a pandas routine for turning a raw table into something you can trust]]></summary></entry></feed>